    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=6,\\dfrac12,-4$.",
      "worked": "Let the roots be $\\alpha,\\dfrac3\\alpha,\\beta$.\n\nSum of roots:\n$$\\alpha+\\frac3\\alpha+\\beta=\\frac52\\qquad(1)$$\nProduct of roots:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha\\left(\\frac3\\alpha\\right)\\beta&=-12\\\\3\\beta&=-12\\\\\\beta&=-4.\\end{align*}$$\nSubstituting $\\beta=-4$ into (1):\n$$\\begin{align*}\\alpha+\\frac3\\alpha+(-4)&=\\frac52\\\\\\alpha+\\frac3\\alpha&=\\frac{13}{2}\\\\2\\alpha^2-13\\alpha+6&=0\\\\(2\\alpha-1)(\\alpha-6)&=0.\\end{align*}$$\nIf $\\alpha=6$, then $\\dfrac3\\alpha=\\dfrac12$; if $\\alpha=\\dfrac12$, then $\\dfrac3\\alpha=6$.\n\nTherefore $x=6,\\dfrac12,-4$.",
